# Maintainer: ArchMage contributors
#
# ArchMage desktop layer umbrella (DESKTOP-01, x86_64).
#
# Desktop stack follows the Omarchy lineage (user decision 2026-11-10):
# Hyprland + uwsm session, Ghostty terminal, waybar, fuzzel launcher,
# gum/fzf TUI tooling — with the ArchMage CN layer and anti-bloat
# discipline. Phone-only packages are deliberately absent: cn-apn (modem),
# archmage-phosh-safety (phosh), archmage-fcitx5-osk (phosh OSK), waydroid
# stack, archmage-btrfs-rollback (phone partition layout). cn-mirror is
# ALARM-specific; the desktop mirror package (archmage-desktop-mirror,
# x86_64 Arch TUNA/USTC) is a follow-up.

pkgname=archmage-desktop
pkgver=2
pkgrel=1
pkgdesc='ArchMage desktop layer umbrella: Hyprland stack + CN defaults + TUI tooling (x86_64)'
arch=(x86_64)
url='https://github.com/Arcane-Reflection/ArchMage'
license=(Apache)
depends=(
  # Omarchy-lineage desktop stack (all in Arch extra; no forking)
  'hyprland'
  'uwsm'
  'ghostty'
  'waybar'
  'fuzzel'
  'xdg-desktop-portal-hyprland'
  'polkit-gnome'
  'brightnessctl'
  # CN defaults (archmage overlay, any-arch configuration packages)
  'archmage-cn-locale'
  'archmage-cn-fonts-meta'
  'archmage-cn-net'
  # CN input method (fcitx5 wayland IME; --wayland-ime per Omarchy 3.0 fix)
  'fcitx5'
  'fcitx5-chinese-addons'
  'fcitx5-gtk'
  'noto-fonts-cjk'
  # TUI tooling layer (v0.2 management face)
  'gum'
  'fzf'
  # Network + audio baseline
  'networkmanager'
  'ufw'
  'pipewire'
  'wireplumber'
  'pipewire-pulse'
  # Browser (Omarchy default lineage)
  'chromium'
)

package() {
    install -d "$pkgdir/usr/share/doc/$pkgname"
    cat > "$pkgdir/usr/share/doc/$pkgname/README" <<'DESCEOF'
ArchMage desktop layer umbrella (Omarchy-lineage stack).

Hyprland (uwsm session) + Ghostty + waybar + fuzzel + fcitx5 CN input +
gum/fzf TUI tooling, on top of the ArchMage CN default configuration set
(locale, CJK fonts, network defaults).

Management happens through the archmage TUI layer (see ROADMAP.md v0.2).
Phone-only layers (modem APN, phosh shell safety, OSK, waydroid, btrfs
rollback layout) are deliberately not pulled in.
DESCEOF
}
